timestamp=2026-11-09T10:31:31.926Z level=INFO run=195d671c message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# For some files, the separator in columns string is semicolon when UTF16LE with tab? Like AA: the column string contains semicolons.\n# Also the actual data for AA has semicolon separation (we saw that). So for files that are UTF16LE, the format is: tab-separated file where fields inside are semicolon-separated? Or just semicolon. Let us read one properly.\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport pandas as pd\n\np = Path('/app/dataset')\n# AA: after skiprows=3, read with sep ';' gave us proper columns split by ;\n# So AA, AC, AE, AG are UTF16LE and semicolon separated\nfor name in ['production_FARM_AA.csv', 'production_FARM_AC.csv', 'production_FARM_AE.csv', 'production_FARM_AG.csv']:\n    try:\n        df = pd.read_csv(p/name, sep=';', encoding='utf-16le', skiprows=3, nrows=0)\n        cols = df.columns.tolist()\n        # look for value col\n        for c in cols:\n            cstripped = c.strip()\n            c2 = cstripped.lower()\n            if any(k in c2 for k in ['reading', 'power', 'yield', 'output', 'meter', 'mwh', 'kwh', 'wh', 'value', 'generation', 'energy']):\n                print(f'{name}: {cstripped}')\n                break\n        else:\n            print(f'{name}: ??')\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f'ERR {name}: {e}')\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
