timestamp=2026-11-09T10:55:20.124Z level=INFO run=195d671c message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let us debug one farm more closely - FARM_D has very large values (1.86M kWh in a day?) That depends on reading type. \n# FARM_D calibration says reading_type is 'power' and unit is 'kw', value_col is 'power_reading' (with space in JSON but we stripped). \n# For power (kW), the energy over a time interval is power * time. If readings are instantaneous power samples, summing without integrating over time is wrong. Or if they are average power over interval, or if they are energy accumulated. We need to infer from data frequency.\n# Look at FARM_D intervals\nfrom read_production import read_production\nimport pandas as pd\ndf = read_production('FARM_D')\n# parse times roughly\n# look at differences\nfor i in range(5):\n    print(df['timestamp'].iloc[i])\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
