timestamp=2026-11-09T10:55:28.919Z level=INFO run=195d671c message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# FARM_D is sampled every 5 minutes. If readings are power in kW (instantaneous/average over interval), then energy per interval = power (kW) * (5/60) hours = power * 5/60 kWh. So total energy = sum of power * interval_hours. That could explain large numbers if we just summed kW values.\n# Also look at other farms. FARM_A has timestamps every 30 min? Let us check FARM_A intervals.\nfrom read_production import read_production\ndf = read_production('FARM_A')\nfor i in range(5):\n    print(df['timestamp'].iloc[i])\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
