timestamp=2026-11-09T10:55:56.827Z level=INFO run=195d671c message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Different sampling rates. The \"energy production\" values depend on whether the reading is power or already accumulated energy. \n# For power readings (kW), we must integrate over time. For energy readings (kWh/Wh/MWh), we sum the energy amounts over the period (or the difference if cumulative). The task says \"real energy production in kilowatt-hours (kWh)\" - so we need to compute total energy. \n# Also look at how values behave: e.g. FARM_D power values - let us see magnitude.\nfrom read_production import read_production\nfrom utils import parse_numeric\ndf = read_production('FARM_D')\n# get value col\nc = {'value_col': 'power_reading'}\nif c['value_col'] not in df.columns:\n    pass\nvals = df['power_reading'].apply(parse_numeric).dropna()\nprint(vals.mean(), vals.max(), vals.min())\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
