timestamp=2026-11-09T10:58:19.598Z level=INFO run=195d671c message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# So FARM_A has 46 readings in the UTC window for 2024-03-15. That makes sense. Let us now check the values - are they cumulative energy (kWh counter) or interval energy? For cumulative, sum of increments would be needed; but if we just sum differences? Or sometimes the reading is the total energy produced so far. Or sometimes interval energy. Let us look at the sequence of values.\nfrom read_production import read_production\nfrom utils import parse_numeric\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfarm_id = 'FARM_A'\ndf = read_production(farm_id)\ntz_name = 'Europe/Warsaw'\nWINDOW_START_UTC = datetime(2024, 3, 15, tzinfo=ZoneInfo('UTC'))\nWINDOW_END_UTC = WINDOW_START_UTC + timedelta(days=1)\n\ndt_utc_list = []\nok_idx = []\nfor i, ts in enumerate(df['timestamp']):\n    s = str(ts).strip()\n    try:\n        dt = datetime.strptime(s, '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')\n    except:\n        try:\n            dt = datetime.strptime(s, '%d.%m.%Y %H:%M:%S')\n        except:\n            continue\n    try:\n        dt_local = dt.replace(tzinfo=ZoneInfo(tz_name))\n        dt_utc_list.append(dt_local.astimezone(ZoneInfo('UTC')))\n        ok_idx.append(i)\n    except:\n        continue\n\ndf_clean = df.iloc[ok_idx].copy()\ndf_clean['dt_utc'] = dt_utc_list\ndf_f = df_clean[(df_clean['dt_utc'] >= WINDOW_START_UTC) & (df_clean['dt_utc'] < WINDOW_END_UTC)]\nvals = df_f['power_reading'].apply(parse_numeric).tolist()\nprint(vals[:15])\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
