timestamp=2026-11-09T11:01:54.947Z level=INFO run=195d671c message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# One is 80.0, one is 0.0. Calibration offset for FARM_D is 80.0. Also the data has patterns like this - the \"actual\" reading vs maybe something else. Or maybe the correct column is the one whose values make sense after calibration? Or look up calibration value more: FARM_D calibration says value_column_name is \"power_reading \" (with space). But both have similar names. Also compare with the other field - maybe the first power_reading is the main one? Or look at the raw data format. Let us look back at FARM_D in the original file structure from earlier? In the full columns when split properly for semicolon files, sometimes the columns get split; but FARM_D is not semicolon. Hmm - let us look at the header line again for FARM_D.\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('/app/dataset') / 'production_FARM_D.csv'\n# try to read raw header\nwith open(p, 'rb') as f:\n    data = f.read(200)\n# decode\nfor enc in ['utf-8', 'utf-16le', 'utf-16be']:\n    try:\n        s = data.decode(enc)\n        print(enc, s[:80])\n        break\n    except:\n        pass\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
